  "id": "Compound::DB01026 - Gene::1584",
  "verbalization": "Ketoconazole and Cyp11b1 share a common pathway through Fluconazole, which binds to Cyp11b1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of CYP11B1 activity. The evidence from Path 1 and Path 2 indicates that Ketoconazole, through its inclusion in the class of Cytochrome P450 3a4 inhibitors and Azoles, ultimately leads to Fluconazole, which binds to Cyp11b1. This establishes a chain of interactions where Ketoconazole indirectly influences Cyp11b1 via Fluconazole. The lowest common ancestors of Ketoconazole and Fluconazole, as well as the shared classification as Anti-Infective Agents and Oxygen Molecular Entities, further support a broad pharmacological context. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Ketoconazole in modulating Cyp11b1 activity through the action of Fluconazole, which is a key mediator in the relationship between the two entities.",
